From 0eda06bdc4fd6b2374a0d4acf03a247bc53ec0be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:06:30 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Pay-first funnel: rebuild landing page, retire free
 registration

Landing page:
- Palette moved to the logo's navy (#010b1b, sampled from icon-512.png) so the
  flattened logo PNG sits on the nav with no visible edge; short navy->darker
  navy hero gradient replaces the navy->orange one that went muddy at the fold.
- Real logo replaces the trophy emoji; wordmark stays live text so the nav stops
  wrapping to two lines (107px -> 53px at 390px, which also fixes the fixed-nav
  overlap of the hero).
- New hero copy leading with the loss, one primary CTA, 'See how it works'
  demoted to a text link, and the captured badge moved above the fold. A 2x crop
  of the title-and-badge region is served below 700px so the badge stays legible.
- Hero split: the navy gradient ends at the headline and everything from the
  subheadline down is dark-on-white. The capture is itself a screenshot of a
  white Amazon page, so framing it in navy read as a bright hole; this also
  lifts the CTA ~86px and leaves the hero band and footer as the only dark
  regions on the page.
  demoted to a text link, and the captured badge moved above the fold. A 2x crop
  of the title-and-badge region is served below 700px so the badge stays legible.
- Proof section moved directly under the hero (was starting 4,555px down on
  mobile). Email subject now matches the badge in the capture, and the
  placeholder Resend sender address is replaced.
- Six feature cards cut to three, emoji icons replaced with inline SVG.
- Pricing cards are now buttons that post to /create_checkout. One 'Most Popular'
  badge instead of two, weekly reframed as 'Launch Week', annual shown as a
  monthly-equivalent, refund policy linked.
- Mobile document height 8,739px -> 6,445px.

Funnel:
- /register retired and 301'd to /#pricing. It was public, unauthenticated, had
  no rate limit, and created a users row from an email and password - the fake
  signup vector. Accounts now come only from a signature-verified Stripe webhook.
- /success renders the password form inline, gated by the verified-paid session,
  and polls /success/setup_status while the async webhook lands. Removes the
  dependency on an emailed link that expires in 24 hours.
- complete_registration.html rebranded (it said 'Amazon Bestseller Monitor' and
  'Create your free account' to people who had just paid), Confirm Password
  dropped, five-rule password policy reduced to 8 characters, enforced server-side.
- Paddle.js removed from pricing.html; checkout is Stripe only.

